      "description": "##### WSUS Client Timestamps Explanation\n\n###### EffectiveLastDetectionTime\n- **Description**: Represents the most recent time the client successfully checked in with the WSUS server to detect updates. This timestamp updates each time a new detection cycle completes and updates are found to be applicable.\n\n###### LastReportedStatusTime\n- **Description**: Indicates the last time the client sent status information to the WSUS server. This includes reports on installed updates, failed installations, and updates that are not applicable. It's pivotal for monitoring the current update status directly from the client.\n\n###### LastSyncTime\n- **Description**: This timestamp shows the last time the client successfully synchronized with the WSUS server. During synchronization, the client retrieves update metadata from the server to assess which updates are applicable.\n\n###### CreatedTime\n- **Description**: This is the time when the WSUS client record was first created on the WSUS server. It essentially marks the initiation of the client's interaction with the WSUS infrastructure.",
