      "description": "##### Vulnerability Ratings and Descriptions\n\n###### Critical\n- **Description**: Exploitation could allow code execution without user interaction, such as through self-propagating malware or when visiting a web page or opening an email.\n- **Recommendation**: Apply Critical updates immediately.\n\n###### Important\n- **Description**: Exploitation could compromise the confidentiality, integrity, or availability of user data, or of processing resources. This includes scenarios where a client is compromised with warnings or prompts, or where sequences of user actions do not generate prompts or warnings.\n- **Recommendation**: Apply Important updates at the earliest opportunity.\n\n###### Moderate\n- **Description**: The impact of the vulnerability is significantly mitigated by factors such as authentication requirements or applicability only to non-default configurations.\n- **Recommendation**: Consider applying the security update.\n\n###### Low\n- **Description**: The impact of the vulnerability is comprehensively mitigated by the characteristics of the affected component.\n- **Recommendation**: Evaluate whether to apply the security update to the affected systems.\n\n###### Unspecified\n- **Description**: Updates for which no specific severity level has been assigned by the update publisher. This could be due to various reasons, such as updates that do not directly impact the security of the system (e.g., minor feature enhancements or non-critical bug fixes).  This typically includes documentation updates, certain non-security related updates, or updates where the severity is not applicable. The absence of a rating does not necessarily indicate the update's lack of importance, but rather that it does not fit into the traditional severity classifications.\n- **Recommendation**: These updates can still be significant for system functionality or user experience. Administrators should review these updates based on the content and the affected components to decide their deployment strategy.\n\nFor more information, please see: [Microsoft Security Update Severity Rating System](https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/msrc/security-update-severity-rating-system)\n",
